files    artifacts/python.wasm.xz, artifacts/python314.zip, artifacts/MANIFEST, THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
built by guest/build.sh in that directory (CPython 3.14.8, WASI SDK 24, Wasmtime 49.0.1 wizer, zlib 1.3.1, SQLite 3.50.4)

python.wasm.xz  xz of a wasm32-wasip1 reactor module: CPython with bashkit_main.c as its entry point, pre-initialized
                with Wizer (the interpreter is already running, common modules imported). Exports memory, bashkit_run.
python314.zip   the standard library as bytecode, plus bashkit's driver (_bashkit_boot) and HTTP shims (requests,
                httpx, http.client over the host bridge). The snapshot cached this zip's directory, so the host must
                serve exactly these bytes at /usr/local/lib/python314.zip.

MANIFEST holds the sha256 of both files; every port checks them before it loads the module. To update: copy the four
files from a newer bashkit commit, change the commit above and the hashes in each port (wasi.py, and the C# and
TypeScript equivalents), and run the three suites.
